  "summary": "A wet drum magnetic separator recovers magnetic particles (for example magnetite) from a slurry. A non-magnetic drum rotates around a stationary magnet arc; magnetic particles are attracted to the drum, carried out of the slurry and dropped into the concentrate launder, while non-magnetic material flows to tailings.",
